    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are `AcceptanceBase` and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner JSON response to include `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nI implemented it at the single idiomatic point where the codebase already derives read-only owner fields from email presence (`membershipLevel`, `locality`), keeping every changed function trivial:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with a setter). No functions changed.\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression line on the existing `toOwnerDto` method:\n  ```java\n  @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n  ```\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** two files, one added annotation line on an existing abstract method (its own body is unchanged, CC stays 1). I avoided introducing a new helper class (which would have added a third file and multiplied the whole cost) and avoided growing the responder functions. Placing it in the mapper also fully satisfies the spec everywhere an owner DTO is returned, not just the GET path the tests exercise, using the exact email-presence idiom already established two lines above.",
